:: The Crack 2 [event main_quest] {"position":"5575,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Access Log" (main_crackLogs), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 4.10, the Monday after The Crack. $ethan.name is completely
   normal. Then the server's access log: every raw log the company has ever recorded was pulled on Saturday night, from the
   login of $darius.name. I confront him. I'm wrong: he spent the weekend out of town, and he can prove it. He's hurt and polite
   about it. If I brought him in at Morale ($flags.dariusBroughtIn) he forgives fast; if I shut him out, it hits harder, and his
   morale with it. Who really pulled the logs is never said; I ask $ethan.name to reset everybody's passwords. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[14].img>><</silent>>
On Monday $ethan.name is the first one in, which never happens. He's brought donuts. He makes a joke about the elevator, and another one about $brian.name's new haircut, and he laughs at his own jokes the way he always does, too loud, slapping the desk. By ten he's arguing with $brian.name about emitter timings at exactly the usual volume.

Whatever I saw through the glass on Saturday, there's no trace of it now. He seems fine, and I decide that he is.

Then I open the server dashboard to check the overnight backups, and there's a line in the access log I don't recognize.

<<linkreplace "Read it">>
Saturday, 21:43: a full export of the raw sensor archive. That's every reading from every unit we've ever run, the diner pilot, $boss.callName's office, the gyms, the Veil tests, and the office vent from the very first day, all packed into one file and downloaded in four minutes.

And next to it, the account that did it, which is $darius.name's.

I sit and look at that for a long time.

<<if $flags.dariusBroughtIn === true>>He has access to the raw data now. I gave it to him myself, the curated version of it, the week of the morale numbers. But I can't think of a reason he'd need to pull the whole archive at night, on a Saturday, in one go, unless he wanted all of it at once without anyone watching, and the archive has things in it that I never cleaned.<<else>>He doesn't even have access to the raw archive, because I shut him out, and now his name is on a full export on a Saturday night when nobody was here. I remember that he kept the printout from that afternoon. He folded it and put it in his jacket instead of the bin, and I didn't think anything of it at the time.<</if>>

<<linkreplace "Call him over">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "$darius.name, can you come to the meeting room for a minute? Now, please." },
{ text: "He looks up, sees my face, and closes his laptop without saving whatever he was working on, which I have never seen him do." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<silently>><<SetBackground $locations[15].img>><</silently>>
I turn the laptop so he can see the log. I'd planned to say something first, but now that he's standing here I don't know how to start, so I just let him read. He reads it standing up, twice.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "That's my account. And unless I'm misreading this, that's the entire archive." },
{ who: $player, text: "Yeah. On Saturday night, when nobody was supposed to be here." },
{ who: $player, text: "Look, I'm just going to ask, okay? Where were you on Saturday night?" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Wait for his answer">>
He doesn't get defensive, which somehow makes it worse. He takes out his phone, scrolls for a moment, and puts it on the table in front of me.

It's a photo of a crowded dining room: a long table, a lot of people in nice clothes, a cake with a big gold 40 on it. $darius.name is in the middle of it in a dark suit, with his arm around a woman who has his cheekbones.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "My cousin's fortieth birthday, in my parents' town, about three hours north of here. I drove up on Saturday morning and came back on Sunday night. You'll notice the photo was taken at 21:38, roughly a minute before I stood up to give a toast." },
{ who: $darius, text: "There's a video of the toast as well, if you need it, although I'd consider it a personal favor if you didn't watch it. Speeches at family gatherings are not among my talents." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I look at the photo, and the timestamp, and his face, which is perfectly calm and has gone a shade paler than usual.

He's telling the truth. He'd be a fool to lie about something this easy to check, and he's anything but a fool. So somebody else used his login, somebody who knew his password, or found it somewhere, or didn't need it in the first place.

<<if $flags.dariusBroughtIn === true>>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Okay. God. I'm sorry, I saw your name next to that this morning and I just... I had to ask." },
{ who: $darius, text: "You did have to ask. I'd think less of you if you hadn't." },
{ text: "He picks his phone back up and puts it in his pocket. He doesn't look away from me while he does it." },
{ who: $darius, text: "In your position I'd have asked the same question, and probably less politely. It looks precisely the way it would look if I had done it." },
{ who: $darius, text: "But a few weeks ago you brought me in and told me the truth when you had no obligation to. I'm not about to throw that away by stealing a file I could simply have asked you for." },
{ who: $player, text: "I know. I'm really sorry, man. I should have just walked over to your desk and asked you like a normal person instead of doing this whole meeting room thing." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Apology accepted. I'd much rather we spend the next ten minutes on who actually did this, because someone in this office has my password, and I would very much like to understand how." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He's hurt, and he's careful not to show it, which is how I can tell. But he's on my side of the table, already thinking about the problem instead of about me. Bringing him in a few weeks ago bought me a lot more today than I ever expected it to.

<<run State.variables.darius.stats.morale = Math.clamp(State.variables.darius.stats.morale - 5, State.variables.darius.stats.min.morale, State.variables.darius.stats.max.morale)>>
<<else>>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "I'm sorry. I saw your name next to it and I... I had to ask." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Of course you did." },
{ text: "He picks his phone back up and slides it into his pocket, very precisely." },
{ who: $darius, text: "If we're finished, may I go back to my desk? The gym report is due at noon, and I'd prefer not to be late with it." },
{ who: $player, text: "$darius.name, wait. I really am sorry, okay? I got this wrong." },
{ who: $darius, text: "There's no need to apologize. You were protecting your company, and I understand that completely." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He means every word of it, and every word is a closed door. He walks back to his desk, opens his laptop, and works through lunch without speaking to anyone. When $sister.callName brings him his coffee, he thanks her the same way he thanks the vending machine.

First I shut him out, and now I've accused him of stealing. I have a feeling that to him those are two data points, and drawing a line between data points is the thing he's best at.

<<run State.variables.darius.stats.morale = Math.clamp(State.variables.darius.stats.morale - 20, State.variables.darius.stats.min.morale, State.variables.darius.stats.max.morale)>>
<<UpdateStat "-" "Morale" 3>>
<</if>>

<<linkreplace "Deal with it">>
<<silently>><<SetBackground $locations[14].img>><</silently>>
Back at my desk I look at the log line again for a while. Saturday, 21:43, on a weekend when the office should have been empty.

I don't let the thought go any further than that. I've had a lot of practice at that since Saturday.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Hey, $ethan.name, can you reset everybody's passwords today? Long ones, and two-factor on the server too. Somebody's been sloppy." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "On it, boss. I'll make them so long that nobody can remember them, you included." },
{ text: "He gives me a thumbs up over his monitor without looking away from his screen, and starts typing." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 1>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
